- **7:** daily, about 15% above the forecast. That is a reasonable amount, but the fees hurt. It is the strongest of the daily plans (p = 0.4).\n- **1:** daily, about 30% above the forecast. That brings write-offs on top of the high fees.\n- **2, 4, 5:** every two days, 12–25% above the forecast. No capacity problems, sensible cushions.\n- **3:** the same product 0 orders as 4. But it orders product 1 once every four days at almost exactly the forecast. That saves no fees, adds storage and makes shortages more likely. So it comes out worse than 4.\n- **0:** every three days, product 0 about 10% above the forecast and product 1 roughly at it. A batch is still sold within its 4-day shelf life. It has the lowest fees.\n\n**Shared losses.** At the start every plan runs short: the opening stock of product 0 (54) covers about a third of the demand for days 0–4, and product 1's stock (26) covers about half of days 0–2. Since this hits all candidates equally, it doesn't change the ranking."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4357, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2313, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4357}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-28T22:37:42.333Z", "request_id": "req_011CgVSDUd7B9aBqx5CdPbiB"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Qp7ZgjcmgqXxPEwNgV1XMe", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "ms